   <titleInfo>
      <title>Baja SAE Competition at Tennessee Tech, 2013</title>
   </titleInfo>
   <abstract>The Baja SAE competition in April 2013 was hosted by Tennessee Technological University in Cookeville, Tennessee, from April 18 to 21. This international collegiate design competition, organized by the Society of Automotive Engineers (SAE), brought together around 100 university teams from across the world to design, build, and race small off-road vehicles. Held at the Hyder-Burks Agriculture Pavilion, the event transformed the grounds into a rugged off-road racecourse featuring hills, woods, and water. Teams were challenged to create a commercially viable vehicle using a standardized engine and four-wheel configuration, with full creative control over all other aspects. Judging was based on cost and design reports, dynamic performance events--including acceleration, maneuverability, sled pull, and suspension--and a demanding four-hour endurance race on a 2.5-mile course. The event also featured collaboration with engineers from companies such as Honda and Polaris, and was praised for its spectator-friendly atmosphere. Information retrieved from https://www.tntechoracle.com/2013/04/04/tech-to-host-baja-sae-tournament/</abstract>
